---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { DailyScreen } from '../components/Daily/DailyScreen'

const title = 'Daily Morse Code Challenge — Same One for Everyone | MorseForge'
const description =
  'One Morse code challenge a day, the same for everyone: eight lines at a set speed, generated from the date. No account, no server, works offline.'
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/daily/">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Daily challenge</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Eight lines at a speed you did not choose, the same for everyone, once a day. One attempt —
      retrying until it went well would make the score meaningless.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <DailyScreen client:load />
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        How is it the same for everyone?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The date is the seed. Every browser runs the same generator over the same UTC date and gets
        the same eight lines, the same speed and the same pass mark — so nothing has to be fetched,
        the challenge works offline, and there is no server that can go down or start charging.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Why UTC and not my day?</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Your practice streak uses your local day, deliberately — going to bed late should not cost
        you Tuesday. A shared challenge is a different question: it only works if today means the
        same thing in Istanbul and in Los Angeles. So the streak is yours and the challenge is
        everyone&rsquo;s.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        I missed the bar. Now what?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Nothing is lost — the streak counts attempts, not passes, because showing up is the only
        thing a streak is any good at encouraging. If the speed is the problem, set your own in
        <a href="/copy/" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-4">copy practice</a> and work up
        to it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
